<title>CHINA: China corn output seen 115.8 million T in 1997.</title>
<headline>China corn output seen 115.8 million T in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-08-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's corn output is expected to reach 115.8 million tonnes in 1997, down by 23.2 million tonnes from last year as a result of drought, the Futures Herald said in an edition available in Beijing on Sunday.</p>
<p>The drought that has affected millions of hectares in the northeast, China's corn basket, was estimated to slash output by more than 20 percent this year, the newspaper said in its August 15 edition.</p>
<p>However, the decline in output was not expected to affect exports, it said, adding that most contracts for the second half of the year had already been signed.</p>
<p>China exported 2.01 million tonnes of corn in the first half, customs figures showed.</p>
<p>-- Beijing newsroom (86) 10-6532 1921; Fax 10-6532-4978</p>
